SUMMARY:SQL Server 2025: The Future of Data Starts Here
DESCRIPTION:Cloud Data Driven\nJoin us to explore the next leap in data pl
 atform technology and learn how to leverage the latest innovations in SQL 
 Server 2025!\n\n🔹 **Overview**\nSQL Server 2025 is more than just an up
 grade. It is a major leap forward that transforms your database into an AI
 -ready powerhouse while delivering modern development tools. This release 
 is packed with innovations designed to redefine performance\, scalability\
 , and productivity across your infrastructure.\n\n🔹 **What will be cove
 red**\nIn this session\, we will dive into demos and practical examples sh
 owcasing a wide range of new enhancements:\n\n(1) Improved **JSON** handli
 ng\n(2) T-SQL **REST API** integration\n(3) Expanded T-SQL **functionality
 **\, including fuzzy string matching and regular expression support\n(4) T
 ime-bound **Extended Events**\n(5) Change event streaming for **real-time*
 * data integration\n(6) Mirroring in **Microsoft Fabric**\n(7) Updates to 
 change tracking and **columnstore indexes**\n\nWhether you are a developer
 \, DBA\, or architect\, this session will help you understand where SQL Se
 rver 2025 fits into your broader data platform strategy.\n\n🔹 **Learnin
 g Objectives**\nBy the end of this session\, you will have a clear underst
 anding of key SQL 2025 features\, including:\n\n✔ Improved JSON handling
 \n✔ T-SQL REST API integration\n✔ Expanded T-SQL functionality\n✔ Ti
 me-bound Extended Events\n✔ Change event streaming\n✔ Mirroring in Mic
 rosoft Fabric\n✔ Advanced change tracking and columnstore index updates\
 n\n🔹 **Level**: Intermediate\n\n**Moderator**: Ronen Ariely \\- Sr\\. C
 onsultant & Data Architect \\| Intl\\. Speaker & Lecturer \\| 7x Former MV
 P \\| Lead: Data Driven Community & GlobalHebrew \\| Data Platforms Expert
 \\.\n\n▬▬▬▬▬ About the community ▬▬▬▬▬\n📌Data Drive
 n Community & Cloud Data-Driven user group\nThe Cloud Data-Driven User Gro
 up is the official user group of the Data-Driven Community\, hosting weekl
 y meetings as part of our community-driven activities. For a full list of 
 upcoming events and more details about our community\, visit: https://data
 drivencommunity.com\n▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬
